 $k \not\equiv 0(\bmod 3)$.
 Since $x=0$ is not the solution of (\ref{key18}), $f(x)=0$ has only one solution in $\mathbb{F}_{q}$
 when $k \not\equiv 0(\bmod 3)$.}
