 %\newline {\bf It should be very careful to say "if and only if"!!!}}
     	
     	Then we prove that $f(x)=a$ has at most one solution in $\mathbb{F}_{q}$ for any $a \in \mathbb{F}_{q}^{*}$ if and only if $k \not\equiv 0(\bmod 3)$.
