 \begin{Th}
\label{th_Tripp4}
 	Let $q=2^{2k+1}$ and $k>0$ be an integer. Then $f(x)=x+ax^{2^{k+1}-1}+a^{2^{2k+1}-2^{k+1}-2}x^{2^{k+1}+1}$, where $a \in \mathbb{F}_{q}$, is a permutation trinomial over $\mathbb{F}_{q}$.
