Let $q = 2^{11}$. Since $2 \cdot 11 = 22 \equiv 1 \pmod{21}$, the Frobenius automorphism $\sigma(x) = x^q$ satisfies $\sigma^2(x) = x^{q^2} = x^2$ for all $x \in K$.

